'' RUN: 'field = N' takes a constant expression, not only a literal: 'field = PK',
'' 'field = ( 1 )', 'field = 1 + 0' and 'field = PK * 2' were ignored and the type laid
'' out unpacked. Output identical to fbc-modern's.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/field-const-expr.bas -o tests/codegen/fieldconstexpr.exe
